\date{2026-08-20}
\title{Segal types are left and right Segal}
\author{fredrikbakke}
\contributor{robschellingerhout}
\meta{source}{[PR\startverb#\stopverb244](https://github.com/samtoth/agda-synthetic-categories/pull/244)}
\tag{changelog}
\import{stt-macros}

\subtree{
\title{Summary}

\p{
We formalise that [Segal types](stt-00AI) [are left](fre-1232)
[and right Segal](fre-1234) by showing that their Hom-families are appropriately
covariant and contravariant. The proof is due to [[robschellingerhout]]. This
resolves a question that we've wondered about repeatedly before. As corollaries we
get that [the Yoneda lemma](Synthetic.Categories.Yoneda) applies to all Segal types,
as well as the strictification operation given in
[[Synthetic.Categories.Strictification]].
}

\p{
The proof uses the
[unital transport characterisation of covariant](fre-1231)/[contravariant](fre-1233)
families: to show a family is covariant/contravariant it suffices to show its fibres
are [#{\Delta^1}-discrete](stt-00B6) and that it has unital transport. We already
know [the Homs of a Segal type are #{\Delta^1}-discrete](stt-00L5) from
[a previous contribution of mine](stt-00L8).
}
}
